# UI registries + official MCPs

Core stack stays **Next.js + anime.js + Canvas UI** (`02-stack.mdc`). Magic UI / Aceternity UI / Skiper UI are **optional additive** kits (effects, sections, uncommon components) — not replacements for the scroll motor or Canvas aesthetic layer.

## Free-only policy (locked)

Use **only free / open registry items** from Magic UI, Aceternity UI, Skiper UI, and Canvas UI.

- **Do not** buy, prompt for, or configure Pro / All-Access / license keys (`SKIPER_LICENSE_KEY`, Aceternity Pro, paid Magic templates, etc.).
- **Do not** install components marked premium / Pro on the vendor site.
- Skiper **free** requires **attribution** to Skiper UI; stay free and credit when a Skiper free component ships.
- Prefer public registry CLI adds. If a CLI add fails with auth/paywall, stop and pick another free item.

## How install actually works (MCP vs deps)

- **MCP** (Magic UI official, or Shadcn for the rest) = discovery for the agent (list / search / read metadata). It does **not** put packages in `node_modules` by itself.
- **Install path** = `npx shadcn@latest add @namespace/name` which (1) copies component source into the repo and (2) installs whatever **npm dependencies** that registry item declares (e.g. motion, cva). There is usually **no** single mega-package `magicui` / `aceternity` / `skiper` for free items.
- **anime.js** stays a normal npm dep (already in `package.json`); no MCP.
- Writers: discover via MCP or docs → `shadcn add` free item → let CLI resolve deps → adapt to typography/story.

## Official MCP map (only these)

| Product | Official MCP? | How agents use it |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Magic UI** | **Yes** — `@magicuidesign/mcp` (Cursor account: Magic UI). Tools: `listRegistryItems`, `searchRegistryItems`, `getRegistryItem`. Docs: https://magicui.design/docs/mcp | Search/get item metadata + source via MCP, then install with shadcn CLI `@magicui/...` |
| **Aceternity UI** | **No standalone** — official path is **shadcn MCP** + `@aceternity` registry. Docs: https://ui.aceternity.com/docs/cli | Use connected **Shadcn** MCP / `npx shadcn@latest` against `@aceternity/...` |
| **Skiper UI** | **No standalone** — shadcn-compatible `@skiper-ui` registry. Docs: https://skiper-ui.com/docs/quick-start | Free items via Shadcn MCP / CLI (no license). Skip premium. Attribution required |
| **Canvas UI** | **Via shadcn MCP** — trusted `@canvas-ui`. Docs: https://canvasui.dev/docs/mcp | Prefer for core aesthetic GPU pieces; Shadcn MCP / CLI `@canvas-ui/...` |
| **anime.js** | **No official MCP shipped** (proposal/PR only). | Never install third-party anime MCP. Consult official anime.js docs for the installed major |

**Forbidden:** community / third-party MCPs claiming Aceternity, Skiper, anime.js, or “Magic Patterns” as Magic UI. **Solo MCP oficiales.**

## `components.json` registries (this repo)

```json
"@canvas-ui": "https://canvasui.dev/r/{name}.json",
"@magicui": "https://magicui.design/r/{name}.json",
"@aceternity": "https://ui.aceternity.com/registry/{name}.json",
"@skiper-ui": "https://skiper-ui.com/r/{name}.json"
```

Install examples (writers, after docs + MCP discover):

- `npx shadcn@latest add @magicui/<name>`
- `npx shadcn@latest add @aceternity/<name>`
- `npx shadcn@latest add @skiper-ui/<name>` (free items only; no license)
- `npx shadcn@latest add @canvas-ui/<name>`

## When to reach for which kit

1. **Scroll / path / timing of the cheese-mouse story** → **anime.js** only (not Framer/Motion from a kit unless the human explicitly okays a one-off).
2. **GPU / liquid / canvas aesthetic over surfaces** → **Canvas UI** first.
3. **Landing-style effects already designed in a kit** (marquee, beams, uncommon chrome) → Magic UI MCP or Shadcn+Aceternity/Skiper — **homage microsite**, do not turn the site into a generic kit demo.
4. Prefer **one kit per surface** over stacking three libraries on the same beat.

## Orchestrator / writer prompts

